tags: functions, databases
---

The new **Postgres with Drizzle** [function template](/docs/products/functions/templates) serves a todo REST API from an [Appwrite Postgres](/docs/products/databases/postgresql) database through [Drizzle ORM](https://orm.drizzle.team/). It is written in TypeScript, keeps the schema in `src/schema.ts` and its SQL migrations in `drizzle/`, and reuses one connection across warm executions through the connection pooler.

Create it in the Console under **Functions** > **Templates** and set `DATABASE_URL` to your database's connection string. The function never changes the schema, so apply the migrations from your machine against the direct port `5432` before the first request:

```bash
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..." npm run db:migrate
```

